{
  "notes": [
    "A college student in a plum crewneck and glasses, a backpack, with a coffee.",
    "States: idle, face-right, face-away-left and face-away-right; walk (a shuffle on the spot), sit (on a chair on the same tile, turned as it is) and type (sitting at the desk in front), walk and type each with -right, -away-left and -away-right, sit with -right (sitting away, give the item the heading); look, laugh, jump (once), dance, wave, write, and angry (red, then fuming: steam from the ears); at work on a line: weld (the near arm out, sparks off what it holds), operate (both arms out, pressing a machine's buttons) and point (the far arm out); on a quest: cast (a staff held high, magic round its tip), strike (a sword raised, then swung out ahead), pray (hands together, eyes shut) and stir (the near arm going round over a pot); busking: play (both arms out round what's held across the front, the near one strumming, to a nod); at the market: sell (both arms out over a counter, handing something over, then a glance up); in a shop: stock (what the near hand holds lifted to a shelf and pushed in); holds, still, for a part that's come off (or anyone): front (the arms flat, pointing forward), overhead (the arms up, the hands on top), out (the arms out to the sides), reach (a long arm pointing forward, to reach in from the frame's edge) and kick (the legs flat, pointing forward). Without a heading of their own, states play at the heading the scene gives the item.",
    "Parts off: groups left-arm, right-arm, arms, left-hand, right-hand, hands, whole-head, left-leg, right-leg, legs. Take a group off with the item's or a key's off, and show it on its own by placing the same person again, hidden, on the same tile, heading and holds, only that group; at the moment, key the person's off and show the part (a cut). Move the part and switch its hold with keys (idle hangs; front, overhead, out, reach, kick). A head and the near arm (left at headings left and away-left, right at right and away-right) take order 1; the far arm, legs and hands -1 (the near hand at left, 1 when it holds something). Held in front of something, place the part on it (at on) with depth front and its order plus one, and move it to where it holds it. Put it back the same way.",
    "Sockets: hair, ears, hat, face and eyes on the head, back on the torso, grip in the near hand and offhand in the far one. A scene swaps what they hold per item (holds), e.g. { \"hair\": { \"object\": \"hair-bun\", \"look\": \"black\" }, \"grip\": \"held-mug\" }."
  ],
